/-!
# A permutation model of the Held group and the surjection from its presented group

This file defines a permutation model `TauCeti.Sporadic.He` of the Held group `He`: the subgroup
of `Equiv.Perm (Fin 2058)` generated by two explicit permutations `He.a` and `He.b`. In the Held
group the maximal subgroups of shape `S₄(4):2` have index `2058`, which is the least degree in
which that group acts faithfully; the model is meant as its action on the cosets of such a
subgroup.

The two permutations are given by their tables of images, and the point `i` of `Fin 2058` is the
point `i` of the source of the tables (see *Provenance*). Products follow Mathlib's convention
`(σ * τ) x = σ (τ x)`. The generators `a`, `b` and their product `a * b` have orders `2`, `7` and
`17`, the orders of the standard generators of the Held group.

The file then shows that Bray's presentation of the Held group, the one carried by
`TauCeti.SporadicName.presentation`, holds in the model: sending the presentation generator of
index `0` to `a` and that of index `1` to `b` makes all seven transcribed relators evaluate to
`1`. No inversion of the generators is needed, because the source derives its tables from this
presentation and states its relations in Mathlib's convention. Extending the assignment gives a
homomorphism from `TauCeti.SporadicName.He.Group` whose range is `He`, hence a surjection onto
`He`; in particular the presented group is nontrivial.

Neither the order of the model nor its transitivity or simplicity is asserted here, and the
surjection is not shown to be injective.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.He`: the permutation model of the Held group on `2058` points.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.He.orderOf_a`, `TauCeti.Sporadic.He.orderOf_b`,
  `TauCeti.Sporadic.He.orderOf_a_mul_b`: the orders `2`, `7` and `17` of the generators and of
  their product.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.He.presentationImage`: the images `a` and `b` of the presentation generators.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.He.lift_presentationImage_toFreeGroup_eq_one`: all seven transcribed relators
  of the presentation of `He` evaluate to `1` at these images.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.He.closure_range_presentationImage`: the images generate the model.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.He.presentationHom`: the homomorphism from the presented group.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.exists_surjective_He`: the presented group maps onto the model.

## Provenance

The tables of `He.a` and `He.b` are those of the permutations `hea` and `heb` of the
`FiniteSimpleGroups` project (Apache-2.0), file `FiniteSimpleGroups/Sporadic/He/Basic.lean` at
commit `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`. That file stores `hea`, `heb` and the inverse of
`heb` as the natural numbers `heaFlat`, `hebFlat` and `hebInvFlat`, the image of the point `i`
being the field `i` of width `12`; the tables below list those fields in order, so the numbering
of the points is unchanged. The source obtained the two permutations by coset enumeration from
Bray's presentation: they are the actions of the generators `a` and `b` on the `2058` cosets of
the subgroup generated by `a`, `b⁻² a b²` and `b² a b⁻²`, the point `0` being that subgroup. The
definitions of the two permutations are taken from the source; its proofs of the order and the
simplicity of the generated group are not reproduced here.

## References

* KitaKen1 (Kenta), *FiniteSimpleGroups*, `He` construction at commit
  `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`,
  <https://github.com/KitaKen1/finite-simple-groups-lean>.
* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, presentation `HeG1-P1`, contributed by John Bray,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/pres/HeG1-P1>.
-/

