a lookup in a list or an array costs one reduction for every position passed.

The definitions are `noncomputable` because the compiler exceeds its recursion depth on tables of
this size, and they are only ever evaluated by the kernel. Their bodies are exposed so that
importing modules can compute with the two permutations. -/

